                <pb facs="0713" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg625"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Scruggs to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-27"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                        1892</hi></date>. (Received September 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Venezuelan Government requests me to ask whether, in case <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Portland</hi> cleared for Trinidad, but proceeded to Puerto Cabello direct,
                    our naval forces can interfere, as desired, in support of court’s decision and
                    strict neutrality.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scruggs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
